        </solution>
        </example>
        
    </page>
    <page>
        <paragraphs>
            <title>Parallel and Perpendicular Lines</title>

            <p component="b" workspace="2in">
                The slope of lines should be able to tell us if they are parllel or perpendicular. What can we learn from this?
            </p>
            <p component="a">
                The slope of lines should be able to tell us if they are parllel or perpendicular. What can we learn from this? Parallel is same slope. Perpendicular product is negative one by thinking about rotating the ilne by 90 degrees.
            </p>
            
        </paragraphs>
    </page>
    <page>
        <definition xml:id="def-parallel-perpendicular">
            <statement>
                <p component="b" workspace="1in">
                    We say that two lines are <term>parallel</term> if:
                </p>
                <p component="a">
                    We say that two lines are <term>parallel</term> if: <ul>
                        <li>
                            <p>
                                Both of them are vertical, or
                            </p>
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <p>
                                They have the same slope
                            </p>
                        </li>
                    </ul>
                </p>

                <p component="b" workspace="1in">
                    We say that two lines are <term>perpendicular</term> if they intersect at a <m>90\deg</m> angle. This can be determined from the slopes by:
                </p>
                <p component="a">
                    We say that two lines are <term>perpendicular</term> if they intersect at a <m>90\deg</m> angle. This can be determined from the slopes by: <ul>
                        <li>
                            <p>
                                A vertical and horizontal line are always perpendicular
                            </p>
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <p>
                                If the products of the slopes is <m>-1</m>.
                            </p>
                        </li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
            </statement>
        </definition>
    </page>
