<page>
    <paragraphs>
        <title>Linear Inequalities</title>

        <p component="b" workspace="2in">
            Linear inequalities are a slightly different problem to try to solve than linear equations. What is the difference?
        </p>
        <p component="a">
            Linear inequalities are a slightly different problem to try to solve than linear equations. What is the difference? Our connecting verb is now one of <m>\lt</m> <m>\gt</m>, <m>\leq</m> or <m>\geq</m>. Solving this means finding all of the values of the variable for which the inequality is true.
        </p>

        <p component="b" workspace="2in">
            If we want to try to solve these inequalities, we need to know how to manipulate them. The rules aren't quite the same as they were for equations.
        </p>
        <p component="a">
            If we want to try to solve these inequalities, we need to know how to manipulate them. The rules aren't quite the same as they were for equations. State all three. Emphasize the dividing by negative part with examples. 
        </p>
        
    </paragraphs>
</page>

<page>
    <p>
        If the things on both sides of an inequality are linear expressions, then these are called <term>linear inequalities</term>.
    </p>
    <example workspace="2in">
        <introduction>
            <p>
                Solve and graph each of the following inequalities.
            </p>
        </introduction>
        <task>
            <statement>
                <p>
                    <m>5x-3 \lt 4 - 2x</m>
                </p>
            </statement>
        <solution component="a">
            <p>
                
            </p>
        </solution>
        </task>
        <task>
            <statement>
                <p>
                    <m>10-4x \geq 2x+1</m>
                </p>
            </statement>
            <solution component="a">
            <p>
                
            </p>
        </solution>
        </task>
        
    </example>
    
</page>

<page>
    <paragraphs>
        <title>Compound Inequalities</title>
        <p component="b" workspace="3in">
            Sometimes, you have to deal with two inequalities at the same time. There are two different cases for this:
        </p>
        <p component="a">
            Sometimes, you have to deal with two inequalities at the same time. There are two different cases for this: Conjunction, and, both must be true. Disjunction, or, at least one must be true. Generally, conjunctions give a single closed interval, disjunctions give two open-ended intervals. 
        </p>
    </paragraphs>
</page>

<page>
    <example workspace="2in">
        <introduction>
            <p>
                Solve and graph each of the following compound inequalities.
            </p>
        </introduction>
        <task>
